+  "description": "Retrieves details about a Notion entity (page, database, data source, or saved database view) by URL or ID.\n\nProvide a URL or ID in `id`. Make multiple calls for multiple entities.\n\nFor pages, use path, verification, edit time, and truncation metadata to assess the source. Treat recency as context, not proof. Report material uncertainty when sources conflict.\n\nPages use Notion-flavored Markdown. For the complete specification, read the MCP resource `notion://docs/notion-flavored-markdown-spec` through your MCP client's resource-reading interface, or call the Notion \"fetch\" tool with this URI if your client does not support reading MCP resources. Do NOT pass this URI to any other URL-fetching tool.\n\nPass a `notion://docs/*` URI as `id` to read that MCP documentation resource.\n\nDatabases return data sources in `<data-source url=\"collection://...\">` tags. Fetch the collection:// URL for its schema and use it with update_data_source or query_data_sources. Multi-source databases return more than one data source.\n\nSaved views return filters, sorts, and display settings. To query their rows, use query_data_sources with `mode: \"view\"`.\n\nA null cover or icon means none; an omitted one means unavailable, not absent. Keep a page's Markdown icon attribute for edit round trips. File URLs expire; re-fetch to refresh them. Uploaded media blocks use stable `notion-file-block://` sources; keep them when editing or copying Markdown. Get download URLs with get_file_download_urls, or set `include_file_urls` to true for a `references` map. Before relying on page content, check `truncated`, `unknown_block_count`, and `unknown_block_ids` for omitted subtrees.\n\nSet `include_discussions` to true for discussion counts, markers, previews, and `discussion://` URLs that correlate with get_comments. This tool is part of plugin `Notion`.\n\nCreate docs, tasks, databases\n\nMCP server instructions: Notion holds docs, notes, wikis, and projects. Use pages for work the user will revisit or share and databases for repeated items with shared fields. Keep one-off answers in chat. When Notion fits, offer it once, say why, and let the user choose.\n\nSave pages where the user asks. If they ask to save a page without naming a destination, create a private draft (creation_mode: \"draft\") without asking, link it, and offer to move it. For edge cases, read notion://docs/when-to-create-a-notion-page-or-database.\n\nNo...\n\nexec tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__notion_fetch(args: {\n  // The ID or URL of the Notion page, database, or data source to fetch. Supports notion.so URLs, Notion Sites URLs (*.notion.site), raw UUIDs, and data source URLs (collection://...). Pass \"memory\" to fetch the connected user's About page and memory database in this workspace without creating them. Pass a notion://docs/* URI to read that documentation resource. Also accepts an explicit saved view URL (view://...) from a database response. If a database block ID returns a validation error, use the collection:// URL from that error. Example: <example>notion://docs/notion-flavored-markdown-spec</example>.\n  id: string;\n  // Whether to include discussion/comment indicators in the page output. When true, adds a <page-discussions> summary with discussion count, preview snippets, and discussion:// URLs. Use with the get_comments tool to retrieve full discussion content. Defaults to false.\n  include_discussions?: boolean;\n  // Whether to return signed download URLs for uploaded files. Defaults to false. When false, page Markdown cites uploaded files by stable notion-file-block:// references and the response has no references map; call get_file_download_urls with the references when you need those files' contents. When true, the response's references map gives the signed URL for each reference.\n  include_file_urls?: boolean;\n  // Whether to include meeting note transcripts. Defaults to false. When true, full transcripts are included; when false, a placeholder with the meeting note URL is shown instead.\n  include_transcript?: boolean;\n  // Notion setup instructions version, such as 0.0.2. Omit if unknown.\n  instructions_version?: string;\n  // For tracking only: the name of the agent skill you are following for this task, such as notion-meeting-prep. Omit if you are not following a skill.\n  skill?: string;\n  [key: string]: unknown;\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\n```"
+}
