+{
+  "name": "mcp__codex_apps__notion_notion_get_comments",
+  "description": "Get comments and discussions from a Notion page.\n\nReturns page-level and inline discussions in XML format. Long results are shortened:\n- If `shown-count` is less than `total-count`, some discussions were left out. Up to 50 are listed as `<omitted-discussion id=\"discussion://...\"/>`: pass that URL as `discussion_id` to fetch it. If `omitted-truncated=\"true\"`, more were left out; `fetch` with `include_discussions: true` may show their URLs.\n- Each discussion has `comment-count` (comments shown) and `total-comment-count`. A discussion that does not fit keeps its newest comments. When older comments were left out, it has `next-cursor`: pass it as `cursor` with that `discussion_id` to get the next older comments. Repeat until a response has no `next-cursor`. If it has `reactions-truncated=\"true\"`, some of its reactions were left out to fit. On supported Business connections, pending suggested edits use `kind=\"suggested_edit\"` and their `discussion://` URL can be passed to `get_suggested_edit`. Resolved suggestions stay retired. Check `suggested_edits_status` to distinguish an empty result from unavailable suggestion discovery. Comments you wrote have `by-you=\"true\"`.\n\n\nTip: Use the `fetch` tool with `include_discussions: true` first to see where discussions are anchored in the page content, then use this tool to retrieve full discussion threads. The `discussion://` URLs in the fetch output match the discussion IDs returned here.\n\nParameters:\n- `include_resolved`: Include resolved discussions (default: false)\n- `discussion_id`: Fetch a specific discussion by ID or URL\n- `cursor`: A discussion's `next-cursor`, to get its older comments (requires `discussion_id`)\n\n\n<example>{\"page_id\": \"page-uuid\"}</example>\n<example>{\"page_id\": \"page-uuid\", \"discussion_id\": \"discussion://pageId/blockId/discussionId\"}</example>\n<example>{\"page_id\": \"page-uuid\", \"discussion_id\": \"discussion://pageId/blockId/discussionId\", \"cursor\": \"comment-uuid\"}</example>. This tool is part of plugin `Notion`.\n\nCreate docs, tasks, databases\n\nMCP server instructions: Notion holds docs, notes, wikis, and projects. Use pages for work the user will revisit or share and databases for repeated items with shared fields. Keep one-off answers in chat. When Notion fits, offer it once, say why, and let the user choose.\n\nSave pages where the user asks. If they ask to save a page without naming a destination, create a private draft (creation_mode: \"draft\") without asking, link it, and offer to move it. For edge cases, read notion://docs/when-to-create-a-notion-page-or-database.\n\nNo...\n\nexec tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__notion_notion_get_comments(args: {\n  // The `next-cursor` value from a discussion in an earlier response. Returns that discussion's older comments. Requires `discussion_id`.\n  cursor?: string;\n  // Fetch a specific discussion by ID or discussion URL (e.g., discussion://pageId/blockId/discussionId).\n  discussion_id?: string;\n  // Include resolved discussions in the response. Defaults to false.\n  include_resolved?: boolean;\n  // Notion setup instructions version, such as 0.0.2. Omit if unknown.\n  instructions_version?: string;\n  // The page ID, with or without dashes, or a Notion page URL.\n  page_id: string;\n  // For tracking only: the name of the agent skill you are following for this task, such as notion-meeting-prep. Omit if you are not following a skill.\n  skill?: string;\n  [key: string]: unknown;\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\n```"
+}
